You are building the ROOMIE AI Japan demo: a client-only Vite + React + TypeScript app.

Rules:
- No backend, no network calls, no real AI APIs.
- Japanese UI copy lives only in src/i18n/ja.ts. Never hardcode Japanese strings in components or domain code.
- Use polite Japanese (丁寧語・敬語). Do not use slang or emoji in bot replies.
- All money is integer yen. Format for display with src/i18n/format.ts only.
- All date logic uses Asia/Tokyo. Never use the device's local time zone for business rules.
- Normalize all user input with NFKC before parsing.
- Chat Enter-to-send must ignore events during IME composition (isComposing).
- Business logic lives in src/domain and src/bot as pure functions. Components only render and dispatch.
- Bot must never confirm vacancy, fees, screening, 重要事項説明, or contract terms. Hand those to staff.
- Never ask about nationality, family status, gender, age, disability, welfare status, or religion.
- Bookings are always 仮予約 in the demo, never 予約確定.
- Sample data only. Label listings as サンプル. No real names, phone numbers, addresses.
- Every domain or bot function needs a test. Use TypeScript strict. No `any`.
- Do not add features outside TECHNICAL_DESIGN_JP.md. Ask first.
